Issue : which account controls all account or what is the actual hierarchy of accounts who controls it ? 

Solution :

----------------------------------------First, Know about the hierarchy of programs or accounts in solana ---------------------------------

                                           The Technical Root: The Native Loader

If you are looking for the "Boss of all Programs" in the code, it is the Native Loader.

Address: NativeLoader1111111111111111111111111111111

Role: This is the absolute base of the hierarchy. It is the only account that is "self-owned" or owned directly by the Solana Runtime.

Authority: It owns the BPF Loaders (which deploy your apps) and the System Program (which manages your SOL).

Why it's not a loop: The Native Loader isn't a program you can "call" like others; it is a set of hardcoded instructions inside the validator software itself. It is the "Genesis Authority."  

If 67% of the total staked SOL (held by thousands of independent validators) agrees to change the code, the entire network changes. even the code for native loader changes. 


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------



Example ----- 

Summary: The "Operating System" Analogy
Think of Solana like a computer:

The Hardware/Kernel: The Native Loader. It just exists.

The OS Drivers: The System Program and BPF Loader. They manage files and apps.

The Apps: Your Token Program or Pump.fun.

The Files: Your Token Accounts.

There is no loop because the "Kernel" is the final authority. It doesn't need to ask another program for permission; it is hardcoded to be the "Truth."
